{"id": "af14b1eb-9ae3-44ef-ad86-78bf0746739b", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "No — the `ListDistributions` response gives you a `DistributionSummary` for each distribution, and that summary doesn't include the `Logging` configuration field at all. It covers things like `ARN`, `Status`, `DomainName`, `Aliases`, `Origins`, `DefaultCacheBehavior`, `CacheBehaviors`, `Enabled`, `ViewerCertificate`, `Restrictions`, `WebACLId`, etc. — but access logging settings (bucket, prefix, enabled, cookie logging) live in the `DistributionConfig`, which is only returned by `GetDistribution` or `GetDistributionConfig` for that specific distribution.

So for an operational review, you'd need to call `GetDistribution` (or `GetDistributionConfig`) per distribution ID to check whether `Logging.Enabled` is true/false — `ListDistributions` alone can't tell you that.

